The easiest way is to use GitHub's built-in license option:

Go back to the repository main page.
Click Add file → Create new file
Filename: LICENSE
Click Choose a license template (if available)
Select Apache License 2.0
Commit the file.

The license must contain these sections/topics:

Definitions
Grant of Copyright License
Grant of Patent License
Redistribution
Submission of Contributions
Trademarks
Disclaimer of Warranty
Limitation of Liability
Accepting Warranty or Additional Liability
